/* ── Shell ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* Real fix (PS-311 — "Accession Number font color is hard to
   read/'terrible.' ... Patient Banner in particular is one of the
   few UI areas with a white background, inconsistent with the rest
   of the app's styling."): confirmed directly — this was a real
   light-on-light bug, not just an aesthetic complaint. This shell
   was still #ffffff while .ps-hb-accession-number/.ps-hb-field-value
   right below it were already set to var(--ps-text-primary)/
   var(--ps-text-muted) (#e2e8f0/#94a3b8) — near-white text on a
   white card. The compact variant of this exact same header
   (.ps-hb-compact, further down this file) already uses the app's
   real, established dark surface tone (#0d1829) with the same light
   text colors and reads correctly; this is that same real fix
   applied to the full (non-compact) header, so both variants finally
