/* Real fix, per direct report: the header itself has no
   justify-content, so with only a title it reads fine, but a title +
   close button just sit side-by-side with the 12px gap instead of the
   close button landing in the corner. Deliberately scoped to the
   close button itself rather than adding justify-content:
   space-between to the header — several of these same headers (e.g.
   confirmation-style "Discard changes?" modals) have only an emoji +
   title and no close button at all; space-between on those would
   incorrectly push the emoji and title apart to opposite corners. */
.ps-modal-dark-header .ps-research-close {
  margin-left: auto;
}

.ps-modal-dark-title {
  font-size: 17px;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #e2e8f0;
