   file. Given a real, established green toggle class family already
   exists (.ps-toggle-track/.ps-toggle-thumb/.ps-toggle-label, used
   elsewhere) but with different colors and dimensions, reusing it here
   would silently change this toggle's look — so this is a new, separate
   `.config-toggle-*` family (matching this file's own `.config-section-*`
   naming) that reproduces the exact current teal appearance.
   Correction (batch 37): this comment previously claimed, based on a
   shallow grep match, that FontsSection.tsx "hand-rolls the identical
   pattern" and that these classes were "ready for it". That did not
   hold up once FontsSection.tsx was actually read in batch 37 — its
   toggle shares this track's 40×22px size and #0891B2 on-color, but has
   a third disabled/greyed state this one doesn't, an 18px (not 14px)
