/* Was a light theme (white/#f8fafc) — the ONE modal in the app that
   never got converted to match everything else. Its own thread text
   colors (#67e8f9, #64748b, #DEE4E7 below) were ALREADY correctly tuned
   for a dark background, which is why near-white body text on a white
   container was nearly invisible -- only the container needed fixing,
   not the text. */
.ps-cmnt-header               { padding: 16px 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(51,65,85,0.9); display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between; flex-shrink: 0; cursor: grab; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); border-radius: 16px 16px 0 0; user-select: none; }
