/* Real fix, item #34: grid columns can't wrap to a new row the way
   flex items can — when the window is too narrow for all three groups
   to fit on one line, the middle "Jump to" cell was being crushed
   rather than the whole row wrapping, producing exactly the
   stacked/overlapping buttons reported. Flex with wrap lets the row
   become two lines gracefully under narrow widths instead. */
.ps-ose-summary-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 8px;
  padding: 8px 0;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
