   .ps-cfgpage-scroll/.ps-cfgpage-inner already use correctly. Without
   this, any tab with enough rows to exceed the viewport (Discordance &
   Reconciliation's 175 records is a clear real-world case) had content
   silently clipped with no way to reach it — not a rendering glitch,
   a hard, invisible cutoff. */
.ps-defic-scroll { flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow-y: auto; width: 100%; }
